  {
    "_id": "a1c2b064-f515-486d-9e12-fe9cefdb22dc",
    "_type": "blogPost",
    "body": [
      {
        "_key": "0c5e5297b665",
        "_type": "youtube",
        "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tJ9fpSRQr9E"
      },
      {
        "_key": "14e43933be1f",
        "_type": "block",
        "children": [
          {
            "_key": "24a7f3827973",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": "I've always wanted to learn Unreal Engine, but on my own terms. I used Houdini where it made sense and treated the project as a technical exercise more than an art piece. With AI tools improving, a lot of conceptual work feels likely to be automated. That pushed me to focus on engineering, parametrics, and robust procedural rules that still matter when AI can do the visuals."
          }
        ],
        "markDefs": [],
        "style": "normal"
      },
      {
        "_key": "7f4994b75a55",
        "_type": "block",
        "children": [
          {
            "_key": "0987b007847c",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": ""
          }
        ],
        "markDefs": [],
        "style": "normal"
      },
      {
        "_key": "11ce9aacba4b",
        "_type": "block",
        "children": [
          {
            "_key": "11fbb0850242",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": "I also wanted the result to feel personally relevant. I live in Singapore. Generic brick-and-window generators are uninspiring to me. So I made a shophouse generator that reflects what I actually see and care about."
          }
        ],
        "markDefs": [],
        "style": "normal"
      },
      {
        "_key": "0bc8aeeff451",
        "_type": "block",
        "children": [
          {
            "_key": "45993bb421a8",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": "\nSo here is a concise breakdown on how this was achieved."
          }
        ],
        "markDefs": [],
        "style": "normal"
      },
      {
        "_key": "701115e0b4fe",
        "_type": "block",
        "children": [
          {
            "_key": "8acfffa64366",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": "\nNot going to go over everything because well... just look at this node tree."
          }
        ],
        "markDefs": [],
        "style": "normal"
      },
      {
        "_key": "f344b8b2244c",
        "_type": "image",
        "asset": {
          "_ref": "image-2d05c2de5ce273f221dd36443c6b0ee935a6f5d7-576x540-png",
          "_type": "reference"
        },
        "caption": "Node hell"
      },
      {
        "_key": "cf5ec34eb31f",
        "_type": "block",
        "children": [
          {
            "_key": "09889364e660",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": ""
          }
        ],
        "markDefs": [],
        "style": "normal"
      },
      {
        "_key": "fd6bfe6cc0e9",
        "_type": "block",
        "children": [
          {
            "_key": "2e0412fd546e",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": ""
          }
        ],
        "markDefs": [],
        "style": "normal"
      },
      {
        "_key": "f0d8ea592868",
        "_type": "block",
        "children": [
          {
            "_key": "3685f80c8360",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": "Start/Inputs"
          }
        ],
        "markDefs": [],
        "style": "h3"
      },
      {
        "_key": "8dea717d4086",
        "_type": "block",
        "children": [
          {
            "_key": "a4993557f535",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": "I decided have an input that most Unreal users would like, the Unreal Cube."
          }
        ],
        "markDefs": [],
        "style": "normal"
      },
      {
        "_key": "46f0b803d09c",
        "_type": "block",
        "children": [
          {
            "_key": "964b882a52d3",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": ""
          }
        ],
        "markDefs": [],
        "style": "normal"
      },
      {
        "_key": "a85eddd15db7",
        "_type": "block",
        "children": [
          {
            "_key": "eef2fcbb91f1",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": "The HDA was first built for Houdini, then adapted for Unreal. I transform the cube by deleting every face but the bottom and flipping it into a flat, segmented plane. Users can choose a plane with size and segment controls or feed their own cube to produce a shophouse. A single switch toggles the behaviour."
          }
        ],
        "markDefs": [],
        "style": "normal"
      },
      {
        "_key": "1f8130614aa4",
        "_type": "image",
        "asset": {
          "_ref": "image-e3928941dd1f652683630b760022d676816749f4-428x375-png",
          "_type": "reference"
        }
      },
      {
        "_key": "b06ad6e3e4cc",
        "_type": "block",
        "children": [
          {
            "_key": "1c3d627edf77",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": "Two detail attributes drive almost everything. One stores the storefront/front angle. The other is the cross product with world up to identify side walls. Those attributes generate groups that control roof slopes, pipe direction, placements, and more. They are the backbone of the HDA."
          }
        ],
        "markDefs": [],
        "style": "normal"
      },
      {
        "_key": "b0e11c3ce9f1",
        "_type": "block",
        "children": [
          {
            "_key": "98c0600e2402",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": ""
          }
        ],
        "markDefs": [],
        "style": "normal"
      },
      {
        "_key": "5495d59c804d",
        "_type": "block",
        "children": [
          {
            "_key": "bada071fc177",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": ""
          }
        ],
        "markDefs": [],
        "style": "normal"
      },
      {
        "_key": "5d650bfb56dc",
        "_type": "block",
        "children": [
          {
            "_key": "2d128ff5af5e",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": "Basic Design Rules"
          }
        ],
        "markDefs": [],
        "style": "h2"
      },
      {
        "_key": "ae7379c7c04e",
        "_type": "image",
        "asset": {
          "_ref": "image-9a70e0115c7e9a3a59f524e253b5768d1d01c05f-1500x783-png",
          "_type": "reference"
        },
        "caption": "Shophouse storefronts (Source: EdgeProp)"
      },
      {
        "_key": "79812057d1dd",
        "_type": "block",
        "children": [
          {
            "_key": "c603e0369992",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": "So the main thing about a shophouse in singapore is the storefront. The ground floor all have a very determined look, which is an inset from whichever direction is considered the front and then a door and windows.\n\nCuriously the doors are always in the middle for the residentials but once they became stores, obviously people more or less placed the doors where ever they wanted, so i chose that instead because it looked less stale.\n"
          }
        ],
        "markDefs": [],
        "style": "normal"
      },
      {
        "_key": "5459bafd0288",
        "_type": "block",
        "children": [
          {
            "_key": "b6ee02941743",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": "Determining where the doors and windows were was just simply resampling the planes, with the detail attributes of where the front is, only populate the door once at that group of points with rand(). Nothing fancy there. Then all you need is a copy to points with the target points selected."
          }
        ],
        "markDefs": [],
        "style": "normal"
      },
      {
        "_key": "af3df4003b08",
        "_type": "image",
        "asset": {
          "_ref": "image-712ba757e6da084003f1c3d3d2db0fad73b2dc9f-771x503-png",
          "_type": "reference"
        },
        "caption": "Doors and Windows"
      },
      {
        "_key": "323d1bd43f29",
        "_type": "block",
        "children": [
          {
            "_key": "91bf381ff6c6",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": "Walls were simple enough, just lots of polyextrudes and booleans with geometry that were created upstream before they became windows and doors, just boxes.\n\nMatch size was used very liberally in this project (there are 32 of them in total) to make sure everything was of the same height/above the grid so that booleans worked correctly."
          }
        ],
        "markDefs": [],
        "style": "normal"
      },
      {
        "_key": "d530210d9049",
        "_type": "block",
        "children": [
          {
            "_key": "27f158d038e8",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": ""
          }
        ],
        "markDefs": [],
        "style": "normal"
      },
      {
        "_key": "36fb9dcf8caa",
        "_type": "block",
        "children": [
          {
            "_key": "5415736778cf",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": "Honestly that's most of the project, in terms of doors and windows, it's all just liberal use of resampling from the edges of the inputs, grouping the points based on the detail attribute for the angle, random attributes on the points, copy to points and then booleans if needed."
          }
        ],
        "markDefs": [],
        "style": "normal"
      },
      {
        "_key": "c1d51729ecd1",
        "_type": "block",
        "children": [
          {
            "_key": "36541ab1a096",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": ""
          }
        ],
        "markDefs": [],
        "style": "normal"
      },
      {
        "_key": "bf962ef663e1",
        "_type": "block",
        "children": [
          {
            "_key": "983682e20447",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": "Even the duplication of floors was done with copy to points, just creating points*floor height for every primitive input and duplicating the entire middle floor piece upwards to the desired height."
          }
        ],
        "markDefs": [],
        "style": "normal"
      },
      {
        "_key": "3f3d200e991b",
        "_type": "block",
        "children": [
          {
            "_key": "6bcf205673d8",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": ""
          }
        ],
        "markDefs": [],
        "style": "normal"
      },
      {
        "_key": "8e96ef0f4ebe",
        "_type": "block",
        "children": [
          {
            "_key": "e5701b370b47",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": "Ok with the simple stuff out of the way, let's just go through my favourites"
          }
        ],
        "markDefs": [],
        "style": "normal"
      },
      {
        "_key": "df2b86043a12",
        "_type": "block",
        "children": [
          {
            "_key": "e2ea782f4341",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": ""
          }
        ],
        "markDefs": [],
        "style": "normal"
      },
      {
        "_key": "9059f5d90f41",
        "_type": "block",
        "children": [
          {
            "_key": "cec4150fd6a0",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": ""
          }
        ],
        "markDefs": [],
        "style": "normal"
      },
      {
        "_key": "fd9715135f19",
        "_type": "block",
        "children": [
          {
            "_key": "b7f1226462a3",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": "Multiparm Unreal Material Randomizer"
          }
        ],
        "markDefs": [],
        "style": "h2"
      },
      {
        "_key": "3bf7646bcf86",
        "_type": "image",
        "asset": {
          "_ref": "image-fdabbb5655bff6d716772d8eeb0553507f1d8f26-759x669-png",
          "_type": "reference"
        }
      },
      {
        "_key": "4b41b400854c",
        "_type": "block",
        "children": [
          {
            "_key": "e9a8fafea4b2",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": "This is my absolute favourite piece of code that I did after looking at many ODforce threads."
          }
        ],
        "markDefs": [],
        "style": "normal"
      },
      {
        "_key": "9ce3d1fa2d6c",
        "_type": "block",
        "children": [
          {
            "_key": "4eb797a1bc57",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": "In short, it randomizes the unreal engine material by a multiparm parameter on the HDA with the amount of parameters you add to the multiparm evenly. "
          }
        ],
        "markDefs": [],
        "style": "normal"
      },
      {
        "_key": "7d6473572f64",
        "_type": "block",
        "children": [
          {
            "_key": "99a4bf0b8fec",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": "So 2 parameters is a 50% chance each, 4 is a 25% chance and so on. IIt’s elegant and it works in Unreal Engine via Houdini Engine."
          }
        ],
        "markDefs": [],
        "style": "normal"
      },
      {
        "_key": "e1ec88ae2404",
        "_type": "block",
        "children": [
          {
            "_key": "e74f7adfab63",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": ""
          }
        ],
        "markDefs": [],
        "style": "normal"
      },
      {
        "_key": "b88e9f6fb3c0",
        "_type": "block",
        "children": [
          {
            "_key": "f9cf3913f900",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": ""
          }
        ],
        "markDefs": [],
        "style": "normal"
      },
      {
        "_key": "81b2df6bb7e2",
        "_type": "block",
        "children": [
          {
            "_key": "8df5aba04f0b",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": "Pipe and Trough Combo"
          }
        ],
        "markDefs": [],
        "style": "h2"
      },
      {
        "_key": "081012536d7f",
        "_type": "block",
        "children": [
          {
            "_key": "db0c2b44590b",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": "Harder problem."
          }
        ],
        "markDefs": [],
        "style": "normal"
      },
      {
        "_key": "30c7e04eba5f",
        "_type": "block",
        "children": [
          {
            "_key": "362261ace0f9",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": "I needed pipes and troughs that respect neighboring building heights. Troughs cannot float above a lower neighbor."
          }
        ],
        "markDefs": [],
        "style": "normal"
      },
      {
        "_key": "4a58a0eecaae",
        "_type": "block",
        "children": [
          {
            "_key": "6bdfb6be67bc",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": "So what I wrote was this that ran over all the possible points for the pipes to decide their direction."
          }
        ],
        "markDefs": [],
        "style": "normal"
      },
      {
        "_key": "084be2b553a9",
        "_type": "image",
        "asset": {
          "_ref": "image-2295e05ef7d849957f58c29aacb8a040395b4f2a-456x173-png",
          "_type": "reference"
        }
      },
      {
        "_key": "370dbf32b96c",
        "_type": "block",
        "children": [
          {
            "_key": "f1a99bf86078",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": "Then grouped 1 in every 2 points to be split out. "
          }
        ],
        "markDefs": [],
        "style": "normal"
      },
      {
        "_key": "f4e6d22da78c",
        "_type": "image",
        "asset": {
          "_ref": "image-58bc810a8f014620667f9bc685592323b66cfb7e-1306x631-png",
          "_type": "reference"
        }
      },
      {
        "_key": "576ad4779d78",
        "_type": "block",
        "children": [
          {
            "_key": "0d4fbbbb27e9",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": "Those were either going to be deleted or verticle signboards. Then did another random delete on the pipe points to reduce it even further."
          }
        ],
        "markDefs": [],
        "style": "normal"
      },
      {
        "_key": "f7faf03932e3",
        "_type": "block",
        "children": [
          {
            "_key": "b9f9081f90ad",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": "After that it's good old copy to points and match size yet again to align the meshes."
          }
        ],
        "markDefs": [],
        "style": "normal"
      },
      {
        "_key": "88c16d06bca2",
        "_type": "block",
        "children": [
          {
            "_key": "883330b7b94a",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": "For the pipes, all they are is clipped pillar curves with a sweep, with the clip directions set by the detail attribute for storefront angle (see, I really used it everywhere)."
          }
        ],
        "markDefs": [],
        "style": "normal"
      },
      {
        "_key": "1010487c25c4",
        "_type": "block",
        "children": [
          {
            "_key": "c4c9084b8de9",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": ""
          }
        ],
        "markDefs": [],
        "style": "normal"
      },
      {
        "_key": "1cf1f068247c",
        "_type": "block",
        "children": [
          {
            "_key": "de753ae9aa63",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": ""
          }
        ],
        "markDefs": [],
        "style": "normal"
      },
      {
        "_key": "805d9a91557f",
        "_type": "block",
        "children": [
          {
            "_key": "d7a741e1cc40",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": "Roof"
          }
        ],
        "markDefs": [],
        "style": "h2"
      },
      {
        "_key": "4b5bbcabda80",
        "_type": "block",
        "children": [
          {
            "_key": "84c248e3bcc3",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": "Roof tiling was tricky. The roof isn’t fully parametric."
          }
        ],
        "markDefs": [],
        "style": "normal"
      },
      {
        "_key": "7649be184332",
        "_type": "block",
        "children": [
          {
            "_key": "4ed7b540d8ae",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": "It's a standard plane to bricker configuration, but the main problem comes with brickering and because there are these \"blockers\" on the roof between each unit, I didn't want the tiles to intersect those."
          }
        ],
        "markDefs": [],
        "style": "normal"
      },
      {
        "_key": "17d3ece39c0d",
        "_type": "image",
        "asset": {
          "_ref": "image-f52107ac20ea23c81bafcdd4c5d96b2683c9ea70-3264x2448-png",
          "_type": "reference"
        },
        "caption": "(Source: wikipedia)"
      },
      {
        "_key": "2e40c021ef54",
        "_type": "block",
        "children": [
          {
            "_key": "accb4b7c7300",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": "But the tiles won't be perfectly the size of those \"blockers\" since I allow for adjustments to how many tiles there can be on either axes."
          }
        ],
        "markDefs": [],
        "style": "normal"
      },
      {
        "_key": "754381e099fd",
        "_type": "block",
        "children": [
          {
            "_key": "a63b1123a92c",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": "In the end I used bounds from the \"blockers\" as a intermediate solution to group the points that are in the volume and left it as that. "
          }
        ],
        "markDefs": [],
        "style": "normal"
      },
      {
        "_key": "0811ebd49a2b",
        "_type": "image",
        "asset": {
          "_ref": "image-4cb776d70c72fcc103207804d749abbd55a73c65-1264x645-png",
          "_type": "reference"
        }
      },
      {
        "_key": "c5e6900922d7",
        "_type": "block",
        "children": [
          {
            "_key": "b87094f5f995",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": "It’s not perfect. It’s a pragmatic compromise that avoids tile/blocker intersections."
          }
        ],
        "markDefs": [],
        "style": "normal"
      },
      {
        "_key": "c20fb7e4f6dd",
        "_type": "block",
        "children": [
          {
            "_key": "edcaa579485d",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": ""
          }
        ],
        "markDefs": [],
        "style": "normal"
      },
      {
        "_key": "f5bba7300cc6",
        "_type": "block",
        "children": [
          {
            "_key": "f0b91a7a1895",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": ""
          }
        ],
        "markDefs": [],
        "style": "normal"
      },
      {
        "_key": "5c02aeaedc8c",
        "_type": "block",
        "children": [
          {
            "_key": "a49cb42040b4",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": "Unreal Engine integration and limits"
          }
        ],
        "markDefs": [],
        "style": "h2"
      },
      {
        "_key": "5e3ca19b9c78",
        "_type": "block",
        "children": [
          {
            "_key": "345fa63fa9e8",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": "Houdini Engine behaved far better than I expected. Multiparm parameters worked in Unreal. The drawback is this HDA does not use true UE instances, so scene load is heavy. There’s plenty of optimization left. If you want a production-ready generator you need to convert parts to instanced meshes and copy it to the correct locations with working uvs."
          }
        ],
        "markDefs": [],
        "style": "normal"
      },
      {
        "_key": "c94c145d0e2d",
        "_type": "block",
        "children": [
          {
            "_key": "fda46b0c0d55",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": ""
          }
        ],
        "markDefs": [],
        "style": "normal"
      },
      {
        "_key": "14e0c423da0b",
        "_type": "block",
        "children": [
          {
            "_key": "b2293a668ef9",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": ""
          }
        ],
        "markDefs": [],
        "style": "normal"
      },
      {
        "_key": "6e391ddbdcf4",
        "_type": "block",
        "children": [
          {
            "_key": "32b6cb574005",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": "Conclusion"
          }
        ],
        "markDefs": [],
        "style": "h2"
      },
      {
        "_key": "5ca27f270ad0",
        "_type": "block",
        "children": [
          {
            "_key": "bff2b4b0e64f",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": "This shophouse HDA proved a clear and practical approach to procedural design. Core systems work well and the tool is useable. Time to close this chapter and start a new project."
          }
        ],
        "markDefs": [],
        "style": "normal"
      }
    ],
